{"file":{"content":"\\begin{conjecture}[Bounded-level multiplier nondegeneracy]\\label{conj:mult}\nThere exist $c_0$ and a finite set of cycle pairs in the level-$c_0$ graph whose\n\\emph{witness elements}\n$W=(\\prod_{\\gamma_1}F)^{L_2}(\\prod_{\\gamma_2}F)^{-L_1}\\in U_{3^c}$ satisfy: for\nevery $c\\ge c_0$ and every primitive $\\chi$ of conductor $3^c$,\n$\\max_W\\lvert\\chi(W^2)-1\\rvert\\ge\\delta_0>0$. (Coboundary multipliers have all\nsuch invariants equal to $1$, so this is uniform distance from the coboundary\ntorus in holonomy form.) The strongest form, supported by the audit below: the\n$W^2$ generate the \\emph{full} principal-unit group of $U_{3^c}$.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Conditional uniform gap]\\label{thm:condunif}\n\\cref{conj:mult} implies $\\sup_c\\gamma_c(s)<1$ for each $s\\in[0,1]$, hence with\n\\cref{thm:collapse} a uniform $\\kappa_Q\\ge\\kappa>0$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}[Proof, modulo \\cref{conj:mult}]\nBy \\cref{thm:descent} (iterated), $\\gamma_c=\\rho(N)/W$ for an operator $N$ at\nfixed level $3^{c_0}$ whose entries have the moduli of the principal operator up\nto exponentially small tails, and whose phases have cycle holonomies\n$\\chi(W^2)$ as above. Since descent is exactly isospectral, only spectral radii\nare compared---no eigenvector conditioning enters. The matrices $N$ range over a\ncompact family at fixed dimension; by Wielandt's equality theorem,\n$\\rho(N)=W$ on a limit point would force the phases to be an exact coboundary,\nmaking every holonomy invariant equal to $1$ and contradicting the uniform\nseparation $\\delta_0$. Hence $\\sup\\rho(N)<W$ over the family.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\subsection*{Holonomy audit}\n\nThe audit runs in exact integer arithmetic on the $F$-elements","filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex","numLines":30,"startLine":897,"totalLines":1117},"type":"text"}